# OpenMS ElutionPeakDetection: run the internal parallel-for only at the top level.
# Called from inside speXtract's window loop (8 concurrent windows), the bare `#pragma omp
# parallel for` spawned 8 nested EPD teams that fought over the program-global named critical
# OPENMS_ElutionPeakDetection_mtraces -> 195M voluntary context switches, 34,858 s system time
# (37% of all CPU) on an S30 run. `if(!omp_in_parallel())` keeps EPD parallel for the top-level
# MS1 call and serial-internal for the nested MS2 calls. MEASURED: system time 34,858 -> 664 s,
# context switches 195M -> 177k, total CPU -28%. NOTE: wall time did NOT improve (~flat) -- the
# contention was threads BLOCKED, not burning wall, and serial EPD loses detection parallelism.
# A throughput/CPU-cost win, not a latency win.
--- src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/ElutionPeakDetection.cpp
+++ src/openms/source/FEATUREFINDER/ElutionPeakDetection.cpp
@@ detectPeaks(std::vector<MassTrace>& mt_vec, ...) @@
 #ifdef _OPENMP
-#pragma omp parallel for
+#pragma omp parallel for if(!omp_in_parallel())
 #endif
